Add trie service: consumes hammertime.hot-ip.v1 and applies each HotIpAdded/HotIpRemoved to the trie and the address's attribute record in one step, serving GET /healthz, GET /readyz and GET /metrics on HAMMERTIME_TRIE_QUERY_BIND (default 0.0.0.0:8081)
Trie service replays hammertime.hot-ip.v1 from the oldest retained record on every start and reports ready only once the replay has reached the log end as it stood at startup; a replay that outlasts HAMMERTIME_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_S fails the start
Add HAMMERTIME_TRIE_FAMILIES (default ipv4): the address families the trie service holds; a hot-ip event for any other family is skipped and counted
Aggregator counts an observation message whose request_count, sequence or window_seconds is outside the range schemas/observation.v1.json allows as malformed (observations_rejected) and skips it, instead of applying it, diverting it as window_too_long, or stopping and crash-looping on its redelivery (a negative request_count, or one large enough that the resulting window count cannot be encoded)
Aggregator counts an observation message whose integer field holds a string, boolean, fraction or infinity as malformed (observations_rejected) and skips it, instead of coercing the value or, for an infinity, stopping
Aggregator shard leases identify the process, not just the member: a second process started under the same HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_MEMBER_ID is refused (shard_held_by_same_member, then start_failed), and a replacement after an unclean stop waits up to HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_LEASE_TTL_S for its predecessor's leases to lapse instead of taking them over at once
Reference compose file sets container_name on the aggregator, so docker compose up --scale aggregator=N is refused
BREAKING: the event log is NATS JetStream; HAMMERTIME_BUS_KIND accepts nats (default) or memory instead of kafka, and HAMMERTIME_BUS_BROKERS is a comma-separated list of NATS server URLs (nats://host:4222) instead of Kafka bootstrap addresses; streams must be created with hammertime-provision before any service starts
BREAKING: HAMMERTIME_SHARD_IDS is required and static: all, or an explicit set within 0..127 that is disjoint per aggregator member; auto is rejected at startup and consumer-group assignment no longer exists
Reference deployment runs nats:2.15.0-alpine with JetStream instead of Apache Kafka; deploy/docker-compose.redpanda.yml is removed; a one-shot provision service creates the streams before the services start and make up waits for every container to be healthy
Aggregator refuses to start when another live member holds one of its shards (shard_owned_elsewhere, exit 1) and stops when its shard lease lapses (shard_lease_lost); add HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_MEMBER_ID (default hostname) and HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_LEASE_TTL_S (default 30)
Aggregator acknowledges a redelivered copy of an observation it already handled under its current claim without applying it again (redelivered_observation)
Every published event carries Nats-Msg-Id = event_id, so the event log drops a retried duplicate inside its 120 s duplicate window
Log bus_endpoints (bus URLs without userinfo) in the starting record in place of bus_brokers
Add hammertime-provision: a one-shot CLI (--servers, --replicas, --timeout) that creates or reconciles the JetStream stream of every registered topic before the services start; exit 0 when every stream matches, 1 when the servers stay unreachable or a stream conflicts on an immutable field, 2 on invalid arguments
Reference deployment runs Apache Kafka (KRaft) and Valkey instead of Redpanda and Redis; every image is pinned; Redpanda remains available via deploy/docker-compose.redpanda.yml
Reject a malformed HAMMERTIME_REDIS_URL at startup as invalid configuration (config_invalid, exit 2) instead of failing inside start() with exit 1; checked only when HAMMERTIME_STORE_KIND=redis
Add aggregator service: consumes hammertime.observations.v1 per shard, maintains per-IP sliding windows, and emits HotIpAdded/HotIpRemoved with weight in attributes
Aggregator diverts late, future, expired-bucket and over-long-window observations to hammertime.observations-reconciliation.v1 and counts them in late_messages/observations_rejected
Aggregator persists each shard's HOT IP set (memory or Redis under hammertime:agg:*) and inherits it on restart or shard handover with a one-window warm-up
Aggregator settings: HAMMERTIME_SHARD_IDS accepts auto (default) or an explicit partition set; HAMMERTIME_SHARD_COUNT is removed; add HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_COMMIT_INTERVAL_S, HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_MAX_TRACKED_IPS, HAMMERTIME_AGGREGATOR_REEVALUATION_BATCH
Bus consumers accept an assignment listener and an optional static partition set on subscribe; an empty static set is rejected with ValueError before any broker call, while group-managed assignment of no partitions stays valid; the in-memory bus assigns its single partition 0
Add a durable per-shard aggregator HOT set and monotonic transition sequence in Redis keys hammertime:agg:{shard}:hot and hammertime:agg:{shard}:seq, which carry no TTL and require maxmemory-policy noeviction (an allkeys-* policy silently loses the HOT set); a recorded transition never moves the shard's sequence backwards
BREAKING: hammertime.observations.v1 has 128 partitions instead of 32, raising the aggregator parallelism ceiling to 128 workers; an existing topic must be recreated at the new count, which remaps every IP to a different partition and invalidates any persisted per-shard state
A dedup-store credential Redis rejects now fails ingest startup on the first attempt instead of being retried until HAMMERTIME_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_S expires
Add GET /readyz to ingest, answering 200 once startup has completed and 503 with {"status":"starting"|"stopping"} otherwise; POST /v1/observations answers the same 503 while the service is not ready
Ingest re-reads HAMMERTIME_CONFIG_PATH every HAMMERTIME_CONFIG_POLL_INTERVAL_S (default 1) and applies a document only when its config_version is strictly greater than the version in force; a document that fails to load or validate is logged and ignored, leaving the previous version in force
Ingest exits 2 when its configuration is invalid, 1 on a runtime failure and 0 after a clean drain; it now retries an unavailable bus or store at startup up to HAMMERTIME_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_S (default 60) and drains within HAMMERTIME_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_S (default 8) on SIGTERM/SIGINT, logging structured starting/ready records
Return 401 with a uniform body for every failed agent authentication; 403 is now only a correct credential for a disabled agent
Throttle failed agent authentication per source prefix and per attempted agent_id, answering 429 with Retry-After
Charge the ingest rate limiter per distinct observed IP as well as per request; over-budget batches get 429 with Retry-After
Drop zero-count observation entries before fan-out; they are no longer published
Agent registry loader and hammertime-agent-token reject a JSON registry/envelope document with a duplicate key anywhere in it (e.g. two entries for the same agent_id) instead of silently keeping the last occurrence; the loader also rejects a previous_token_expires_at value without an explicit UTC offset instead of assuming UTC
hammertime-agent-token accepts `--key-file PATH` as an out-of-band alternative to `--key` on every subcommand that reads the deployment key; `hash --allow-weak` now warns to stderr, `migrate` refuses to overwrite a non-empty `--out` unless `--force` is passed, and a missing or malformed registry/envelope file is reported as a clean error instead of a traceback
BREAKING: agent registry stores HMAC-SHA-256 token hashes in config/agents.v2.json (registry_version 2) instead of plaintext tokens; set HAMMERTIME_INGEST_AGENT_TOKEN_KEY, convert the old file with `hammertime-agent-token migrate`, and repoint HAMMERTIME_INGEST_AGENTS_PATH before upgrading
Add `hammertime-agent-token` for generating agent tokens, writing their hashes into the registry, rotating a credential with a bounded overlap window (previous_token_hash plus a required expiry), and migrating a v1 plaintext registry
Add optional `attributes` to HotIpAdded/HotIpRemoved events, validated against schemas/ip_attributes.v1.json (registered names attributes_version/weight, x_-prefixed experimental keys, 1024-byte/16-key caps); absent attributes encode byte-identically to before
Add `weight_function` and `weight_max` config keys to detection_config, reserved for the fixed-point weight a future aggregator change will write into an IP's attributes at HOT/COLD transition
Reject observations whose sequence exceeds 9223372036854775807
Ingest claims an observation's (agent_id, sequence) atomically before publishing it, closing a race where concurrent retries of the same request could all be accepted; a retry after a 503 publish failure is now reported as a duplicate (200) rather than retried immediately, until the claim's dedup window lapses
BREAKING: event envelopes carry an optional `subject` that participates in event_id derivation; builds without it reject such envelopes as event_id mismatches
Ingest publishes accepted observations to hammertime.observations.v1 as one message per IP, keyed by that IP, returning 503 if publishing fails and 202 only once all of them are durably recorded; repeated IPs within one message are summed
Add ingest service: POST /v1/observations validates against schemas/observation.v1.json, rejecting malformed IPs, unaligned window_start, and oversized bodies/observation arrays with 400/413; accepted requests return 202 but are not yet published (no dedup/bus/auth wiring). Add GET /healthz liveness check and a placeholder GET /metrics
Add in-memory and Kafka-backed message bus (Producer/Consumer) with a canonical topic registry (hammertime.hot-ip.v1, observations, observations-reconciliation, prefix-stats), keyed by IP except prefix-stats which is keyed by prefix
Add event envelope and JSON codec for RequestObservation/HotIpAdded/HotIpRemoved/PrefixStatsChanged, with a deterministic event_id derived from (agent_id, sequence, event_type) for idempotent redelivery
